<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Carthach of Lismore</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/637">637</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Saint Mochuda, Carthach the Younger</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Carthach, also called Mochuda, was an Irish monk and saint who died in 637. He founded and ruled a monastery at Rahan in the midlands but was expelled from there around 636 and led his community south to Lismore, in the lands of the Déisi. His foundation at Lismore became one of the most famous schools of early Ireland, and he is venerated as its patron.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/carthach-of-lismore.jpg" alt="Carthach of Lismore" width="320" height="292" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Andreas F. Borchert · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lismore_Carthages_Cathedral_Altar_Tomb_E_2007_08_03.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
